#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179548 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/id #uuid "3a28f359-71aa-5b9b-b55c-802374e6821f" :question/math-academy-id "e-8745" :question/problem "Calculate $\\nabla\\times(3\\mathbf{F} + \\mathbf{G})$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = 3x\\,\\mathbf{i} + y^2z\\,\\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}, \\quad (\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{G})(x,y,z) = 3y^2\\,\\mathbf{i} + 4z\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\times \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =∇\\times (3F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3x & {y}^{2}z & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x)]k \\\\  & =(0-{y}^{2})i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3[-{y}^{2}\\,i]+[3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k] \\\\  & =-3{y}^{2}\\,i+3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =(3{y}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =4z\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,1,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-1,1,0) & =4(0)\\,j+k=k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179550 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "e27e6735-4d50-5c26-a20d-44454ddcdef3" :question/math-academy-id "e-8931" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) =  \\langle 0, y-z, x-y\\rangle$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z) = x+y.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times \\mathbf F = \\langle 0,\\,-1,\\,0\\rangle, \n\\quad\n\\nabla f = \\langle 1,\\, 1,\\, 0\\rangle,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F)$ at the point $(-1,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F) = f \\nabla \\times \\mathbf {F}+   \\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & y-z & x-y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (y-z)]\\,i-[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (0)]\\,j+[1\\cdot (y-z)-1\\cdot (0)]\\,k \\\\  & =(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j+(y-z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x+y)⟨0,-1,0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-(x+y),0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,-2x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(-1,1,3) & =⟨(-1)-1,\\,-2(-1),\\,1-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd57de8-9613-5a2d-b250-1256e758fcdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366838} {:answer/id #uuid "c7c75d6b-cf75-544e-b91d-ce8ce69634d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-3\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366839} {:answer/id #uuid "9676ca3b-a8bf-5169-b714-9f4c43df824b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366840} {:answer/id #uuid "7b2c6bbe-a185-592a-8dbf-f13ee1a9cd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i+2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366841} {:answer/id #uuid "90f8d1f8-016d-523f-b081-bc76f0d11212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7c75d6b-cf75-544e-b91d-ce8ce69634d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-3\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366839} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc4e76b2-9e53-585b-b42d-cd7facc74bf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f694a45-bb80-5fc5-bc87-30958ae2f792" :question/math-academy-id "q-105711" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F-G)$ at the point $(0,2,1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\,i+xy\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=-i+2z\\,j-x\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡z & 0 & xy\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(0)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)]k \\\\  & =(x-0)i-(y-\\frac{1}{z})j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =x\\,i+(\\frac{1}{z}-y)j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G \\\\  & =x\\,i+(\\frac{1}{z}-y)j-[-i+2z\\,j-x\\,k] \\\\  & =x\\,i+(\\frac{1}{z}-y)j+i-2z\\,j+x\\,k \\\\  & =(x+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{z}-y-2z)j+x\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,2,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(0,2,1) & =(0+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{1}-2-2(1))j+0\\,k \\\\  & =i-3\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3df17644-84e9-5490-9a46-e21ae8d3b3cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366845} {:answer/id #uuid "2734c944-dc51-5802-8c7b-f65c2498e403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i-3\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366846} {:answer/id #uuid "17483ec0-7c0a-540e-92d1-d728c39f27ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366847} {:answer/id #uuid "4a934b73-4c26-5600-b8f6-04d31b2de547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i+4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366848} {:answer/id #uuid "6640ab9d-dc7f-5c52-867f-9e77c070d6b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2734c944-dc51-5802-8c7b-f65c2498e403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i-3\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366846} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ef56c19-5bdd-55b2-961c-455e339ce25d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c99c802-9c0a-555e-905b-2fc17880a001" :question/math-academy-id "q-105713" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F+G)$ at the point $(4,3,-1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=-3\\,i+z\\,j+8\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{k},\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=-i-j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ -3 & z & 8\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(8\\sqrt{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8\\sqrt{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-3)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-3)]k \\\\  & =(0-1)i-(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-i-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =-i-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,j+[-i-j] \\\\  & =-i-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,j-i-j \\\\  & =-2\\,i-(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}+1)j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(4,3,-1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F+G))(4,3,-1) & =-2\\,i-(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{4}}+1)j \\\\  & =-2\\,i-3\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22b1f7e6-4442-5e2a-a841-c7b32ae47e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488541} {:answer/id #uuid "58ec558c-d6f3-58e0-9b30-c9079a8514c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i-8\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488639} {:answer/id #uuid "94698b03-5cff-5cf9-93a7-70a660e8ea1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,j+5\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488769} {:answer/id #uuid "c21e913d-8c60-59fd-a2f7-ee60ea0be642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488862} {:answer/id #uuid "d05504c9-446a-5857-96c3-6d98b995534b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58ec558c-d6f3-58e0-9b30-c9079a8514c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i-8\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488639} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e1827e-bb95-5b76-9c80-da8e23a83f9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8edc0c0-9a3d-5546-8149-aa1e5f0446b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-105791" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (4F+G)$ at the point $(0,1,-1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=y{e}^{x}\\,i+xz\\,j+(y-1)\\,\\text{k},\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=z\\,i.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =∇\\times (4F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ y{e}^{x} & xz & y-1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{e}^{x})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x})]k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i-(0-0)\\,j+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =4(∇\\times F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4[(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k]+z\\,i \\\\  & =4(1-x)\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k+z\\,i \\\\  & =[4(1-x)+z]\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,-1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (4F+G))(0,1,-1) & =[4(1-0)+(-1)]\\,i+4(-1-{e}^{0})\\,k \\\\  & =[4-1]\\,i+4(-1-1)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,i-8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abc12917-c767-5961-875f-8b79c0ea4558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177137} {:answer/id #uuid "08afb4e5-f12f-5c39-8a4d-af1df6ce9745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i-5\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488491} {:answer/id #uuid "5c3feea7-809e-5194-b77d-2a337acc1747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488649} {:answer/id #uuid "79d18dc1-c0bb-50e7-a72e-25cf91922adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488712} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f59412-f61c-5a93-9b03-097a20b5443f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2f59412-f61c-5a93-9b03-097a20b5443f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488901} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eade32f-b760-5926-93db-b12fa72570ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffa5f452-f601-5e92-9491-4a18ed51c649" :question/math-academy-id "q-105798" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F-G)$ at the point $(-2,0,3)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=z{e}^{y}\\,i+3\\,j-x\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=2x{e}^{y}\\,i-2{e}^{y}\\,j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ z{e}^{y} & 3 & -x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z{e}^{y})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z{e}^{y})]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-((-1)-{e}^{y})j+(0-z{e}^{y})k \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k-[2x{e}^{y}\\,i-2{e}^{y}\\,j] \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k-2x{e}^{y}\\,i+2{e}^{y}\\,j \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{y}\\,i+(3{e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-2,0,3),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-2,0,3) & =-2(-2){e}^{0}\\,i+(3{e}^{0}+1)\\,j-3{e}^{0}\\,k \\\\  & =4\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067e0099-a214-57d4-869c-c70c94a82c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,0,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488485} {:answer/id #uuid "675820df-6ea9-5f30-9192-0ae8291264b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488669} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa35d43-0a5c-5368-b9f4-e38bbe3647e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488681} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a645d3-a518-5b55-bd59-e07fe9e39994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488874} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d9f5c3-101a-532e-8e93-6d12cddd64ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "675820df-6ea9-5f30-9192-0ae8291264b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488669} :answer-field/id #uuid "87266618-2882-52b8-96d1-51f6b11cd2c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f311fcaa-7f7c-50da-9066-652f1bc7fb5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105897" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x{e}^{y},z,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=x-{e}^{y}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨-1,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨1,-{e}^{y},0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(2,0,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{y} & 0 \\\\ x{e}^{y} & z & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[-{e}^{y}(0)-0(z)]i-[1(0)-0(x{e}^{y})]j+[1(z)-(-{e}^{y})(x{e}^{y})]k \\\\  & =0\\,i-0\\,j+(z+x{e}^{2y})\\,k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x-{e}^{y})⟨-1,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}-x,0,x{e}^{2y}-{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}-x,0,2x{e}^{2y}+z-{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(2,0,-3) & =⟨{e}^{0}-2,0,2(2){e}^{2(0)}+(-3)-(2)^{2}{e}^{0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dcb20c5-ace4-5356-918e-a260adfc5b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488533} {:answer/id #uuid "3e626866-926c-5638-8514-10fe8911bfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-8,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488598} {:answer/id #uuid "62f0f666-5714-5bdd-ac2c-a5c2b0a1ad02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,-1,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488660} {:answer/id #uuid "67b3423e-e4b7-56ef-b64b-3bde9aa959ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,4,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488671} {:answer/id #uuid "ce34e2bd-fa56-525d-9e23-0ce1549d6ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,4,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e626866-926c-5638-8514-10fe8911bfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-8,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488598} :answer-field/id #uuid "cee411fe-3c0d-5c7d-9c42-5d9b1df29d7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c76b758-88c8-5667-93d2-dbb6a9e1da40" :question/math-academy-id "q-105956" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\sqrt{x},0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=-z.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,0,-1⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(4,1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ z & \\sqrt{x} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(0)-(-1)(\\sqrt{x})]i-[0(0)-(-1)(z)]j+[0(\\sqrt{x})-0(z)]k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\,i-z\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(-z)⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-2z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(4,1,4) & =⟨\\sqrt{4},-2(4),-\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-8,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "406d7fc1-59b5-57a2-93cd-988d48533d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,4,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488604} {:answer/id #uuid "543874d6-b5ec-5cf9-ad85-65e957697883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488631} {:answer/id #uuid "c7002173-662f-590e-85c4-bebb1d460e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,4,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488876} {:answer/id #uuid "d35ebd08-4a97-5d01-9b27-dd8017794e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,3,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488903} {:answer/id #uuid "f00a9184-3171-5cc7-9fb6-e28f4ae84e39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7002173-662f-590e-85c4-bebb1d460e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,4,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488876} :answer-field/id #uuid "36ec198d-cd51-504c-b007-6c8fdb361499" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69db9a7c-5652-51d3-8060-5596c178f982" :question/math-academy-id "q-105958" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨0,{e}^{3x},2y⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=2x+3.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨2,0,3{e}^{3x}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨2,0,0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(0,-1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3x} & 2y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(2y)-0({e}^{3x})]i-[2(2y)-0(0)]j+[2({e}^{3x})-0(0)]k \\\\  & =0\\,i-4y\\,j+2{e}^{3x}\\,k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4y,2{e}^{3x}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(2x+3)⟨2,0,3{e}^{3x}⟩+⟨0,-4y,2{e}^{3x}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2(2x+3),0,(6x+9){e}^{3x}⟩+⟨0,-4y,2{e}^{3x}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2(2x+3),-4y,(6x+11){e}^{3x}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,-1,4) & =⟨2(2(0)+3),-4(-1),(6(0)+11){e}^{3(0)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,4,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b5033ae-e9b3-5d47-b65e-9b2087d2b8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238440} {:answer/id #uuid "5a7e1336-d218-5bab-af5f-5db4a021be48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,-2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238836} {:answer/id #uuid "adbfa1f7-56c2-56f2-8e8d-059420e4d718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,2,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239562} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf0d2de-df09-508e-92e8-67f3c6320633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239693} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb316d6-5409-5a1d-a42e-5287e7b1d5e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b5033ae-e9b3-5d47-b65e-9b2087d2b8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238440} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd7c6d3-a5bf-5348-a990-e86743a44d17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ccf254f7-98f8-509b-bf14-7e75e519ef48" :question/math-academy-id "q-105960" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,0,z⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{x}{y}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,0,-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x⟩,\\,∇f=⟨\\frac{1}{y},-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}},0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(1,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} & 0 \\\\ y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & 0 & z\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}(z)-0(0)]i-[\\frac{1}{y}(z)-0(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)]j+[\\frac{1}{y}(0)-(-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}})(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)]k \\\\  & =-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{z}{y}\\,j+\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{y}⟨0,0,-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x⟩+⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,-\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩+⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,1,3) & =⟨-\\frac{1(3)}{(1)^{2}},-\\frac{3}{1},0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9abc8ad-f39e-5fc6-90d9-653da6babbab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\,i+5\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388218} {:answer/id #uuid "7768dac4-d868-5afd-bda4-43bbcf7b1aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388219} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab09299-49d2-52a5-a29c-ad5903348ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388220} {:answer/id #uuid "bda2b6dc-21a1-5460-af1d-428180dcd5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,i+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388221} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf18e2e-e02b-5026-ab11-05f919114a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\,j+5\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbf18e2e-e02b-5026-ab11-05f919114a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\,j+5\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388222} :answer-field/id #uuid "785f634a-3bb0-5c9e-b015-ebbcf506a3c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5669465a-097d-533e-a021-36c62b5eb0bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-131434" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (2F+G)$ at the point $(-1,2,0)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=xyz\\,i+xy\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=xy\\,j-x\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F+G) & =∇\\times (2F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =2∇\\times F+∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ xyz & xy & {z}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xyz)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-xy)j+(y-xz)k \\\\  & =xy\\,j+(y-xz)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F+G) & =2∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =2[xy\\,j+(y-xz)\\,k]+xy\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =2xy\\,j+2(y-xz)\\,k+xy\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =3xy\\,j+(2y-2xz-x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,2,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (2F+G))(-1,2,0)=-6\\,j+5\\,k.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266091 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0100d61e-bd3a-57c3-ac46-ef0541e36274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263010} {:answer/id #uuid "2042f10b-c030-5440-b613-21a9c012d3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263295} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e6b082-e166-5ac8-86bc-ab551fbc182d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264961} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d5658b-f678-5414-8532-e4f1e07ce37d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265169} {:answer/id #uuid "f923aa32-197d-5f20-bcd7-cb503c0d99f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1e6b082-e166-5ac8-86bc-ab551fbc182d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264961} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8585553-bc3d-59dd-bec0-062d6e8ffbec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ded29f1-5616-5a96-a16e-84431dafd500" :question/math-academy-id "q-131473" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,y,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=xyz.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩,\\,∇f=⟨yz,xz,xy⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(1,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ yz & xz & xy \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡z & y & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[(xz)(0)-(y)(xy)]i-[(yz)(0)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)(xy)]j+[(yz)(y)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)(xz)]k \\\\  & =-x{y}^{2}\\,i+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,j+(z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =xyz⟨0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩+⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-xyz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩+⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},-xyz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},-xy(z\\operatorname{sin}⁡z-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z),z({y}^{2}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,1,0) & =⟨-1,-(0\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
